{ id:"passive", icon:"🔄", title:"Passive Voice", cat:"Grammar", level:"Intermediate", questions:[
["Choose the correct passive form of: “Someone stole my bicycle.”",["My bicycle is stole.","My bicycle was stolen.","My bicycle has stole.","My bicycle was steal."],1,"Past simple active becomes was/were + past participle: “was stolen”."],
["“They are building a new bridge here.” → The passive form is:",["A new bridge is being built here.","A new bridge is built here yesterday.","A new bridge was being built here.","A new bridge has being built here."],0,"Present continuous passive = is/are being + past participle."],
["“She has written three novels.” → In passive:",["Three novels are written by her.","Three novels have been written by her.","Three novels has been written by her.","Three novels were being written by her."],1,"Present perfect passive = have/has been + past participle."],
["“The head teacher will announce the results tomorrow.” →",["The results will announced tomorrow.","The results will be announced tomorrow.","The results would announced tomorrow.","The results are announce tomorrow."],1,"Future passive = will be + past participle: “will be announced”."],
