["“He gave me a useful book.” → The passive form is:",["A useful book gives me.","I was given a useful book.","I am give a useful book.","A book was giving to me."],1,"With two objects, one passive can start with “I”: I was given a useful book."],
["The active form of “The window was broken by the strong wind” is:",["The strong wind was breaking the window.","The strong wind broke the window.","The strong wind has break the window.","The window broke the strong wind."],1,"Past simple passive “was broken” returns to active past simple “broke”."],
["“You must finish this work today.” →",["This work must be finished today.","This work must finished today.","This work must is finished today.","This work must been finished today."],0,"Modal passive = modal + be + past participle: “must be finished”."],
